From lamj@stat.cmu.edu  Mon May 14 11:35:27 2001
From: Johnny C. Lam <lamj@stat.cmu.edu>
To: tech-pkg@netbsd.org
Date: Mon, 14 May 2001 11:35:27 +0000
Subject: PostgreSQL update

I've updated PostgreSQL in pkgsrc to 7.1.1.  One of the changes I
introduced was splitting the package into separate client/server
packages.  All platforms, including the mips platforms, should now be
able to install at least everything but the postgresql-server package.
For now, the postgresql-server is restricted only to non-mips
platforms (until someone writes a TAS implementation for MIPS).  This
is good because an hpcmips machine should now be usable as a
PostgreSQL client.

I'd be interested in hearing reports from alpha users, as there have
previously been problems with PostgreSQL on NetBSD/alpha.  I'd like to
know if the update fixes any old problems.

